      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "Two constraint families will be designed: (1) Rigid (low-dimensional) — analytic constraints that force a unique solution (e.g., linear equality constraints on function values at w points), predicting N_c(w) ~ constant or decreasing as w increases (small capacity suffices); (2) Fat (high-dimensional) — constraints that allow continuous solution families (e.g., inequality constraints or underdetermined systems), predicting N_c(w) increasing with w (larger capacity needed to avoid violations). The phase transition w_c will be identified where N_c(w) drops sharply in the rigid case or rises sharply in the fat case. At least 3 random seeds per w will be used to compute mean±std of N_c(w)."
